package cyfr:process@0.1.0;

/// A session on a program: lines in, sequence-numbered lines out.
/// The program is the one a `login` need of the catalyst's manifest is
/// bound to by consent; it runs in its own box, never in the component.
/// A session belongs to the program and the catalyst's key, not to one
/// run: a later run opening the same key attaches to it while its program
/// runs. Each run opens before it sends, reads or closes. An error is a
/// code: `denied`, `setup_required`, `busy`, `ended`, `invalid_request`,
/// `too_large`, `unavailable` or `lost`.
interface pipe {
    /// An open session, and whether its program was already running for
    /// the key (`resumed`) or was started for this open, in which case a
    /// catalyst speaking a protocol over it starts that protocol again.
    record opened {
        session: string,
        resumed: bool,
    }

    /// One line the program wrote, numbered in its session's sequence.
    record line {
        seq: u64,
        text: string,
    }

    /// The lines past the sequence number a `recv` named, how many lines
    /// the session's buffer dropped, and whether its program still runs.
    record recv-result {
        lines: list<line>,
        dropped: u32,
        running: bool,
    }

    /// Open a session on the program the `login` need `need` is bound to,
    /// under the catalyst's `key` for it (the chat request's session or a
    /// fresh id), running the program's command with `argv` appended.
    /// Returns ok(opened) or err(code). An open with a key whose session
    /// still runs attaches to it.
    open: func(need: string, key: string, argv: list<string>) -> result<opened, string>;

    /// Write `lines` to the session's program, in order.
    send: func(session: string, lines: list<string>) -> result<_, string>;

    /// Read the lines past the sequence number `after`, waiting at most
    /// `max-wait-ms` for one when there is none. A line is kept until a
    /// later call names a higher `after`, so a repeat answers the same
    /// lines; an answer carries as many as fit, and the next call names
    /// the last one it got. A session no longer held answers no lines and
    /// `running: false`.
    recv: func(session: string, after: u64, max-wait-ms: u32) -> result<recv-result, string>;

    /// End the session and its program.
    close: func(session: string) -> result<_, string>;
}
